#N canvas 20 20 2900 1820 12;
#X text 20 20 u_root -- the root of Cut It. main.pd (the device) and main-dev.pd (the Mac) both instantiate this and nothing else \, so the two entry points cannot drift., f 58;
#X text 2300 20 creation args \, all six required: 1 the Pd channel the nanoKONTROL's own channel 1 lands on (17 on the device). 2 the same for the Launchpad (1). 3 u_state's data directory \, absolute \, no trailing slash. 4 the same as 1 for the SP-404 (33). 5 for the Volca (49). 6 u_net's inbound UDP port. What each is on the Mac \, why 3 and 6 differ there \, and why a wrong count loads in silence: ref/architecture.md \, Creation arguments. inlets: none. outlets: none., f 80;
#X obj 20 340 r~ inL;
#X obj 20 620 throw~ outL;
#X obj 330 340 r~ inR;
#X obj 330 620 throw~ outR;
#X obj 170 400 u_level in-l;
#X obj 480 400 u_level in-r;
#X text 70 490 v0.4: e_chop \, e_pitch \, e_trem \, e_verb go in this gap., f 30;
#X text 20 700 inL is drums (the tip) and inR is fx: the SP-404's hard-panned pair on a TRS Y-cable (item 11)., f 34;
#X text 20 800 C-4, f 58;
#X text 470 1050 A signal fan-out needs no trigger: every signal cord runs every block. C-3 is for messages., f 46;
