#X text 900 1300 The columns are ref/architecture.md's diagram: the m_ layers \, then the buses and the map \, then the display owners. A file with cords sits by its cords instead: u_init's to m_launchpad and u_state (u_init owns when \, they own what) \, u_map's and u_net's to the two output devices (C-2: no bus carries a sounding note) \, g_grid's from m_launchpad (surface ownership) and c_clock (the beat) \, and c_steps between u_map \, m_404 and g_grid (ref/module/sequencer.md)., f 90;
#X obj 20 1200 c_clock 1 8;
#X obj 20 1320 g_grid \$2;
#X text 300 1200 The grid's own clock \, since nothing may assume the global clock is its own (poly-tempo \, ref/module/tempo.md). Ratio 1 and eight beats \, so its beat number indexes the grid's bottom row., f 58;
#X obj 2300 1120 u_net 192.168.1.5 8000 \$6;
#X text 2300 1170 192.168.1.5 is only the fallback: on the Organelle's own access point phone-ip.sh finds the phone itself (ref/device/phone.md)., f 58;
